  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 950 PM CDT Wed May 27 2026\n\nThe active patterns persists into the weekend with medium to high\nrain chances each day. Saturday and Sunday will feature the\nhighest rain probabilities, particularly along and south of I-40,\nwhere additional widespread rainfall is likely. By the end of the\nweekend, cumulative rainfall since the start of the week could\napproach or exceed 2-4 inches for many. Early next week, rain\nchances gradually diminish as the upper trough weakens and high\npressure begins to build into the region. A few isolated showers\nremain possible early in the week, but drier conditions are\nfavored by mid week. Temperatures trend slightly cooler, with\nhighs in the upper 70s to low 80s and lows in the low to mid 60s.",
